<header><p class="enc-kicker">Work / monument · text</p><h1 class="enc-title">Cheitharol Kumbaba</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Cheitharol Kumbaba is the royal chronicle of Manipur, kept by court scribes in the Meitei language and script. It records the reigns of the kings of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ningthouja-dynasty">Ningthouja dynasty</a> year by year, beginning with <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/nongda-lairen-pakhangba">Nongda Lairen Pakhangba</a>, traditionally in 33 CE, and continuing into the 19th century. Its early sections are legendary, but the later entries form a detailed contemporary record.</p></div>
